# The image build only needs the sources, the Makefile and packaging/. Without
# this the context carries the host's build/ directory, whose LTO objects were
# produced by a different gcc than the one in the image; the link then fails
# with a bytecode-version mismatch. CI clones fresh so it never saw this, but
# a local `docker build` did, and shipping host artefacts into an image is
# wrong regardless.

build/
.git/
.cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.codex/
node_modules/
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/
ui/out/
compile_commands.json
daemonization-spec.md
CLAUDE.md
*.o
*.d
*.gcda
*.gcno
